  Why R²(tree_count) is near/below zero:
    On valid (tree) pixels, tree_count = 1–8, median = 1, ~50% of
    pixels equal 1. After log1p the target std ≈ 0.26 — nearly the
    same magnitude as RMSE. SS_tot is therefore tiny, so R² ≈ 0 even
    when RMSE is reasonable. Use RMSE / MAE as the primary metric for
    tree_count; R² is unreliable for this near-constant distribution.
